    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-78661",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-78661"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "When coalescing adjacent text nodes in addText and fosterParent, appending to an existing TextNode's Data via string concatenation (n.Data += text) reallocated and copied the accumulated string on every token. Inputs containing many short text runs separated by ignored end tags (such as \"a\u003c/x\u003e\") caused O(n^2) allocations and byte copies. Accumulate coalesced text in per-node byte slices during parsing and materialize Data strings once at the end of parse.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
